/* book: lead: Delta modulation (DM) is the simplest differential coder: one bit per sample. At each clock tick it compares the input with a staircase built from past bits and sends 1 if the input is higher, 0 if lower; the staircase then moves one step Δ up or down. The hardware is a comparator, a clock and an integrator. Adaptive delta modulation (ADM) changes Δ with the signal slope, which makes DM usable for */
