/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The transmitter keeps a staircase approximation x̃ of the input.
   - One bit per sample, so the bit rate equals the sampling rate.
   - The receiver rebuilds the same staircase from the bits with an accumulator (an integrator in analog form), then a lowpass filter at fm smooths it.
   - The staircase can rise at most Δ per sample, a slope of Δfs volts per second.
   - Δ in volts, fs in samples/s, f the tone frequency in Hz, A the peak amplitude in volts.
   - On a slow or flat input the staircase hunts up and down by Δ around it: granular noise, the DM form of quantization noise.
   - ADM changes the step from the bit pattern.
   - For a tone at the largest amplitude that avoids overload, DM gives SNR = 3fs³/(8π²f2W), where W is the receiver filter bandwidth.
   - Answer.
*/
