/* book Worked example 2: Q: x(t) = sin(2π·500t) V is delta modulated at fs = 8 kHz with Δ = 0.3 V, starting from x̃ = 0. Trace samples 0 to 12 and say where granular noise and slope overload appear.
   1. Rule: b = 1 if x[n] ≥ x̃[n − 1]; then x̃[n] = x̃[n − 1] ± 0.3 V.
   2. Check the slopes first: the input reaches 2π × 500 × 1 = 3142 V/s, the staircase only 0.3 × 8000 = 2400 V/s, so overload is expected near the zero crossings.
   3. n = 3 to 6: around the peak the bits alternate 1, 0, 1, 0 and the staircase hunts between 0.90 and 1.20 V: granular noise.
   4. n = 7 to 12: the bits stay 0 but the error grows to −0.38 and −0.41 V at n = 9 and 10, because the input falls 0.38 V per sample near the crossing and the staircase only 0.30 V: slope overload.
   Answer:  */
