/* book exam traps: DM bit rate is fs, not n fs: one bit per sample. | A larger Δ is not simply better: it removes slope overload but raises granular noise. | Overload depends on the slope 2πfA, not on amplitude alone: a small high-frequency tone can overload while a large slow one does not. | ADM sends no side information; the receiver derives the same steps from the received bits, so Rb is still fs. */
